  "preamble": "Affrication of the palatalized stop [tʲ] to the alveolar affricate [ts], with loss of palatality. The Proto-Slavic soft *ť (from *tj) became c [ts] throughout West Slavic (Czech, Slovak, Polish, Sorbian, Kashubian), while East Slavic has č [tɕ] and South Slavic shows ć, ќ or št. The exact phonetic value of Proto-Slavic *ť ([tʲ] or palatal [c]) is debated.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Affrication, Depalatalization",
  "languageExamples": [
